These are the unit seeds, not the units this machine runs.

scripts/setup.sh copies this directory to installed/quadlets/, and
scripts/link-quadlets.sh links the result into the rootless Quadlet search path.
Edit installed/quadlets/ for a deployment; edit these only to change the default
every install starts from.

@REPO_ROOT@
    A placeholder for this checkout's absolute path, substituted by
    scripts/setup.sh while seeding, so no unit has to assume where the checkout
    lives. It is not a systemd specifier: a `%h/...` path would break as soon as
    the tree is cloned somewhere else, and an unsubstituted @REPO_ROOT@ in an
    installed unit points at a directory that does not exist -- a loud failure,
    not a silent one.

    Everything a unit refers to at run time is therefore under the checkout:
    installed/envars/ for EnvironmentFile=, installed/data/ for Volume=, and
    builds/ for the SetWorkingDirectory= of a .build unit.

Nothing else in this directory is read by Quadlet: the link step selects by
extension (.container, .build, .network), so this file stays out of the search
path after the copy.
